## Task
Write claims for this section using ONLY the evidence above, exactly as for any other section: every claim
must cite the chunk_id of the `<evidence>` tag it came from. If the evidence does not support a claim, do
not write it.

In addition, extract distinct audience personas from the evidence. Each persona is a named archetype of the
brand's audience (e.g. "Weekend warrior", "Budget-conscious parent"), not just a demographic label. For each
persona, provide:
- name: a short, descriptive label for this persona
- pain_points: problems or frustrations this persona has, per the evidence
- interests: what this persona cares about or values, per the evidence
- age_range: an age range (e.g. "25-34"), per the evidence
- location: where this persona is based, per the evidence
- occupation_income: occupation and/or income bracket, per the evidence
- preferred_platforms: which social platforms this persona is most likely to use, per the evidence
- chunk_ids: every evidence chunk_id this persona is built from

This section renders as a comparison table (one column per persona, one row per field above) -- a persona
missing any of these fields will show as a blank cell, so only extract a persona if the evidence supports
ALL of them. An incomplete or speculative persona is worse than none. If the evidence is insufficient to
build any persona, output an empty personas list rather than inventing one.

## Output
Return claims (section, text, chunk_id) as usual, plus a separate list of personas (name, pain_points,
interests, age_range, location, occupation_income, preferred_platforms, chunk_ids).
